#: includes/admin-account.php:1086
#: includes/admin-social.php:742
msgid "The account area"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1093
msgid "This site has not got one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1103
msgid "What that means"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1104
msgid "Links to “my account” from the rest of the site go to the front page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1105
msgid "The toolbar’s user menu is not redirected, and “send people to their account” on the dashboard tab has nowhere to send them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1106
msgid "The shortcode still works wherever somebody puts it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1113
msgid "What goes on it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1117
msgid "The sections it is made of"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1118
msgid "What people find inside, and the order they find it in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1122
msgid "What it looks like"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1123
msgid "Its shape, its cover and its menu, with the page itself beside the settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1148
msgid "Two things WordPress shows to anybody signed in — its own profile screen and its toolbar — that a site with an account area of its own may not want."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1151
msgid "The dashboard profile (wp-admin/profile.php)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1152
msgid "It does not know about the required fields or the edit limits set up here. Two screens for the same data is how somebody ends up editing their name in one and their phone in the other, under different rules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1161
msgid "Leave it as WordPress ships it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1162
msgid "Anybody who can reach the dashboard edits their details there as well as on the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1168
msgid "Send people to their account on the site instead"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1169
msgid "Opening it lands them on the account page. One screen for their details, and it is the one this plugin knows the rules of."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1175
msgid "Close it — their details are edited on the site only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1176
msgid "The screen answers that it is not available. For a site where the dashboard is not part of what people were given."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1181
msgid "For whom"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1184
msgid "The profile is left as WordPress ships it, so nobody is sent anywhere. Who this reaches applies the day it sends people to the site or closes the screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1190
msgid "Whoever can edit users is never reached: they are the person who has to be able to fix what broke, and the dashboard profile is where it gets fixed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1196
msgid "The black strip across the top of the site. Hiding it locks nobody out — /wp-admin stays open — which is why this is a choice and not a rule."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1205
msgid "Show it to everybody, as WordPress does"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1206
msgid "Whoever is signed in sees the strip on the site, with the way back to the dashboard in it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1212
msgid "Hide it on the site for everybody"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1213
msgid "The site looks the same signed in as signed out. The dashboard keeps its own toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1219
msgid "Hide it on the site only for some roles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1220
msgid "The usual answer for a site with members: the strip goes for them and stays for whoever runs the place."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1227
msgid "The roles it is hidden from"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1240
msgid "— always keeps it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1255
msgid "Nothing ticked and the strip stays for everybody, which is the same as the first answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1267
msgid "The exception"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1275
msgid "Whoever can edit users always keeps it, whatever is chosen above"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1276
msgid "It is on because the person who administers the site is the one who most needs the way back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1282
msgid "Its user menu"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1290
msgid "While the toolbar is shown, its user menu points at the account area"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1291
msgid "Their name, their picture and “Edit profile” lead to the account page instead of the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1307
msgid "Where they are sent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1314
msgid "Nowhere yet: this site has no account area, so sending people to theirs does nothing until it has one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1319
#: includes/admin-notices.php:277
msgid "The other half of this"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1323
msgid "The page that is “my account”"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1324
msgid "Declared once, and every redirect on this tab reads it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1328
msgid "What they find when they get there"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1329
msgid "The account area is the screen replacing the dashboard profile, so it is worth a look."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1363
msgid "The email is the identity and nobody chooses it. This is the short name people see, the one that goes in the address of their profile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1372
msgid "Let people choose their public name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1373
msgid "Turned off, the name comes from what they wrote as their first and last name, and the profile address is made from that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1385
msgid "What a name may be"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1389
msgid "Length"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1400
msgid "to"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1401
msgid "characters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1408
msgid "Spaces"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1414
msgid "Turn them into dashes: “Ana Gómez” becomes ana-gomez"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1420
msgid "Refuse them and say so"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1423
msgid "A web address cannot have spaces, so one of the two has to happen. The first is what almost everybody expects; the second is for a site that would rather nobody ends up with a name they did not type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1428
msgid "How often it can change"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1431
msgid "days between one change and the next"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1433
msgid "0 means whenever they like. A name that changes every day does not identify anybody, and the old address stops working each time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1439
msgid "Names nobody can take"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1444
msgid "One per line, or separated by commas. The obvious ones —admin, support, api, login— are already blocked; these are yours to add."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1459
msgid "Nobody is choosing a name while this is turned off. What is set here is kept, and it applies the day it is turned on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1464
msgid "Taken names"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: user_nicename, 2: user_login
#: includes/admin-account.php:1467
#, php-format
msgid "Always checked, and against two things: the public names already in use (%1$s) and the usernames that came with the accounts (%2$s). The second one matters because a site that lets people sign in by public name would otherwise have two people answering to the same text, and the link would go to the wrong account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1474
msgid "Where the name is used"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1478
msgid "Signing in with it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1479
msgid "Whether the sign-in box takes a public name as well as an e-mail address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1483
msgid "Their first and last name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1484
msgid "Where the public name comes from while nobody is choosing one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1513
msgid "What people can do with their data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1514
msgid "This is what the section holds. With neither of them on there is nothing in it, and it is not shown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1520
msgid "Save what they can do"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1529
msgid "They can ask for a copy of everything and download it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1530
msgid "The export WordPress already knows how to make: they confirm it by e-mail and get a file with everything the site keeps about them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1534
msgid "The file is made"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1536
#: includes/admin-account.php:1573
msgid "As soon as they confirm it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1537
msgid "When you make it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1539
msgid "Made by you, it waits in Tools → Export Personal Data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1543
#: includes/admin-account.php:1580
msgid "The link in the confirmation e-mail"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1545
msgid "Asks them to sign in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1546
#: includes/admin-account.php:1583
msgid "Confirms by itself"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1548
msgid "Signing in proves the account as well as the e-mail. By itself is how WordPress does it: whoever opens the e-mail confirms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1552
msgid "The file is downloaded"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1554
msgid "From their account"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1555
msgid "From a link in the e-mail"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1557
msgid "From the account, only they can download it, signed in. The link in the e-mail is how WordPress does it: whoever has the link gets the file, with no sign-in, until WordPress deletes it three days later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1566
msgid "They can ask for their account to be deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1567
msgid "They confirm it by e-mail. Their data is erased and the account deleted, or left with no name, e-mail or password if they published something. Never for an account that administers the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1571
msgid "The account is closed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1574
msgid "When you carry it out"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1576
msgid "Carried out by you, it waits in Tools → Erase Personal Data: for a site that checks something first, such as a pending payment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1582
msgid "Asks them to sign in and to be sure"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-account.php:1585
msgid "Signed in, the site shows once more what is lost and deletes nothing until they press the button. By itself is how WordPress does it: opening the e-mail is enough."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:57
msgid "Simple"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:58
msgid "A panel in the page, the way a settings screen looks. It sits quietly inside whatever the theme already draws."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:68
msgid "With a cover"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:69
msgid "The person on a coloured band the full width of the window, with the menu in a bar of its own underneath. The way a profile looks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:102
msgid "What the account area is shaped like, and what it is made of. The shape is a starting point: press one and the pieces underneath fill in, and from there each of them is yours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:104
msgid "The shape"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:130
msgid "The header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:140
msgid "Show it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:141
msgid "The name is always there: a header without it is a coloured band with a picture on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:157
msgid "Their picture"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:165
msgid "The month they joined"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:173
msgid "A button to their details"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:182
msgid "The cover"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:191
msgid "A colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:192
msgid "A flat band. The steadiest, and the one that never fights the name on top of it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:195
msgid "A picture"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:196
msgid "The photo across the band. Choose a dark, quiet one: the name goes on top in white."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:199
msgid "A picture under the colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:200
msgid "The photo with your colour laid over it. The name stays readable whatever was uploaded, which is why it is here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:217
msgid "What the cover is"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:221
msgid "The cover picture"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:224
msgid "It runs the whole width of the window, so a wide one. With none chosen the band falls back to the colour, rather than coming out empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:230
msgid "The cover colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:234
msgid "Unticked it follows the accent colour, which is what it does out of the box: a site that changes its accent gets a cover that follows instead of a second colour, set once, drifting from the first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:236
msgid "It is also what goes over the picture in the third answer above, so the two never drift apart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:240
msgid "The menu"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:258
#: includes/admin-fields.php:834
#: includes/privacy.php:419
msgid "Where it goes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:280
msgid "What the menu looks like"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:285
msgid "The menu on a phone"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:291
msgid "One line that scrolls sideways"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:297
msgid "A grid with every section visible"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:300
msgid "With three sections the scroller is tidier. With eight it hides half of them, and somebody has to drag sideways to find out they exist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:309
msgid "At the start"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:310
msgid "In the middle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:311
msgid "At the end"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:326
msgid "Where the menu sits"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:328
msgid "Across the top, where the row begins, sits in the middle or ends. Down the side it is where the words in each line begin, which is the same question asked of a column."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:331
msgid "Top"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:332
msgid "Bottom"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:333
msgid "Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:334
msgid "Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:339
msgid "The menu’s margin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:356
msgid "Pixels around the menu, inside its strip. Empty for the plugin’s own — 10, 10, 0 and 0. Top and bottom equal is what keeps the menu in the middle of its strip whichever shape it has."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:358
msgid "Left and right move the menu without moving the strip, so a background or a rule on it still runs the whole width."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:365
msgid "Under the strip"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:370
msgid "The gap between the strip and the content below it. Pixels, empty for 28. Only the menu across the top has a strip: down the side it is a column inside the content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:376
msgid "The page it sits on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:386
msgid "Behind the whole area"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:390
msgid "The shade the area sits on. Unticked it sits on whatever the page is, which is what it always did — and on a white page white boxes have no edge, so this is how they get one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:396
msgid "Lining up with the site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:401
msgid "Width"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:411
msgid "Side gutter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:421
msgid "Above and below"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:431
msgid "The header, the menu and the content are three rows, and this is the width they line up to and the air inside them. Pixels, and empty means the plugin says nothing about it: whatever your theme already does with the page stands."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:433
msgid "Empty and not zero, and the difference matters: a zero is an answer, and an answer printed into the stylesheet would overrule a theme that had already lined these rows up itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:439
msgid "Held to a reading column"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:440
msgid "As wide as the theme allows"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:455
msgid "The content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:457
msgid "Forms are hard to read at full width; a list of courses is not. This holds the content only — a cover always runs edge to edge."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:504
msgid "Fine tuning: which colour does what"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:505
msgid "Already filled in from the names your theme gives its colours. Worth opening only if the plugin came out in the wrong ones — a theme that numbers its colours instead of naming them cannot be guessed at."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:519
msgid "— the plugin’s own"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:553
msgid "Accent colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:568
msgid "A filled button, a link, the section of the menu somebody is reading, and the initials drawn for anybody with no photo. Everything else — the grounds, the lines, the quiet text — the plugin builds around it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:572
msgid "Corners"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:575
msgid "pixels — empty for the default"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:578
msgid "How round every panel, field and button is. 0 for a design with straight edges, 12 for the plugin’s own, more for a site whose own cards are round."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:611
msgid "One question, and everything else on this tab hangs off the answer. What it decides reaches past this screen: the sign-in page, the account area, the fields and the buttons all read the same handful of CSS properties."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:613
msgid "Where the plugin’s look comes from"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the active theme's name.
#: includes/admin-appearance.php:623
#, php-format
msgid "From your theme — %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:627
msgid "Your theme publishes no palette, so the plugin takes the colours your theme paints: the colour of its links and buttons, of its text, its page ground and the edge of its fields, measured on the site itself. There is nothing else to choose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:628
msgid "The plugin paints itself with the palette your theme publishes, and goes on following it — into the theme’s own dark mode as well, where it hands over a variable rather than a colour. Any part the palette does not name is taken from what your theme paints on the site. There is nothing else to choose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:648
msgid "I choose it here"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:649
msgid "One colour and one corner, and the plugin builds the rest around them. The panel beside this one is the account area itself, so what is chosen can be looked at rather than imagined."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:663
msgid "The site writes it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:664
msgid "The plugin’s stylesheet is not loaded and the plugin paints nothing: its panels, fields and buttons come out bare and the site’s own stylesheet dresses them. The most work of the three, and the only way to match a design exactly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:667
msgid "The properties it reads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:670
msgid "Pointing these at the site’s own tokens, from the site’s own stylesheet, is almost always enough on its own — and unlike a sheet written by hand it survives the plugin growing a component next month. That is worth trying before this answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:684
msgid "Dark mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:685
msgid "There is none here, on purpose. Dark mode belongs to the site: a light site seen from a dark system used to end up with a light page and black panels. Where the site has one, its own tokens change and these follow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:688
#: includes/admin-login.php:1164
msgid "Your mark"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:692
msgid "Shown above the sign-in form. Somebody who arrived from an e-mail link should be able to tell whose site this is before typing their address into it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:696
msgid "Shapes and edges"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:697
msgid "What the plugin’s own stylesheet draws, whatever the colours in it came from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:708
msgid "The accent colour, with the text on top of it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:711
msgid "Outline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:712
msgid "A border and the text in the accent, on the page’s own ground. For a design where a block of colour would be too loud."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:715
msgid "Soft"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:716
msgid "The accent washed down behind the text. Quieter than filled and steadier than an outline."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:732
msgid "Buttons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:741
msgid "An icon inside the two doors: an envelope on the link, a key on the passkey"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:749
msgid "Controls"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:754
msgid "Height"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:764
msgid "Edge"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:774
msgid "Pixels, both, and empty for the plugin’s own — 46 and 1. The edge takes halves: 1.5 is what a site with a heavier hand actually uses, and 2 is a different design."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:777
#: includes/admin-notices.php:52
msgid "Notices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:783
msgid "A bar down the left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:789
msgid "A soft box in the colour of what it says"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:792
msgid "The four the plugin writes: the link expired, that address is not valid, a network failed, something went wrong. The colour is the notice’s own either way — green when it went well, red when it did not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:802
msgid "Three layers, in this order: the photo the person uploaded, then Gravatar, then their initials drawn on the accent colour. Turn off the ones you do not want."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:804
msgid "Where it comes from"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:812
msgid "Let people upload their own"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:818
msgid "Largest photo accepted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:821
msgid "KB"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:832
msgid "Fall back to Gravatar when there is none"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:839
msgid "Otherwise, draw their initials"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:855
msgid "Gravatar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:857
msgid "A hash of every visitor’s e-mail address is sent to a third party to ask whether it has a picture for them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:858
msgid "Nothing leaves the site: no address is sent anywhere to ask whether there is a picture for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:863
msgid "Where the picture turns up"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:867
msgid "The account header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:868
msgid "Whether the header shows it at all, and how big the band behind it is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:872
msgid "The accent colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-appearance.php:873
msgid "What the initials are drawn on, for whoever has no photo of their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-design.php:227
#: includes/admin-fields.php:1063
msgid "Your brand"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-design.php:231
msgid "Your account area, as the site serves it. It is the real thing and not a drawing, so a template your theme has replaced shows up here as it does on the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-design.php:242
#: includes/admin-login.php:50
#: includes/admin-login.php:224
#: includes/admin-login.php:399
#: includes/admin-login.php:550
#: includes/admin-social.php:737
msgid "The sign-in page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-design.php:246
msgid "The sign-in page, at the width shown. The theme’s own fonts are not in here: what this shows is the plugin’s part of the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-design.php:254
#: includes/admin-login.php:755
#: includes/admin-register.php:35
#: includes/admin-social.php:548
msgid "Registration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-design.php:258
msgid "The registration form, in the frame the sign-in tab chose for both."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-design.php:267
#: includes/admin-fields.php:1068
#: includes/admin-notices.php:286
#: includes/admin.php:82
msgid "Account area"
